\[ 120^\circ + 150^\circ + m\angle C = 180^\circ \]

Combining the known angle measures, we have:
\[ 270^\circ + m\angle C = 180^\circ \]

To isolate \(m\angle C\), we subtract \(270^\circ\) from both sides of the equation:
\[ m\angle C = 180^\circ - 270^\circ \]
